{
    "background_story": "Rachel was a middle manager at a large corporation, stuck in a comfortable but unfulfilling routine. She was neither exceptional nor struggling, just coasting through her days with a sense of mediocrity. Her work was satisfactory, but never outstanding, and she often found herself wondering if this was all there was to life. Rachel's social life was similarly middling - she had a small circle of acquaintances, but no close friends. Her hobbies were equally uninspiring, consisting of watching TV and browsing social media. Despite her desire for something more, Rachel struggled to break free from the inertia that had become her life. She felt like she was just going through the motions, never truly excelling or failing, just existing in a state of perpetual averageness.",
